{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1u4tveEsTgLzbi2EDq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Build it, with a randomized holdout built in. More research first isn't worth the delay.**\n\n**Why build:**\n- The email test is strong evidence. It was randomized, used pharmacy records as the outcome, and had about 400 patients per arm. The 13-point drop (31% to 18%) has a rough 95% interval of about ±6 points, so even the pessimistic end is a meaningful gain.\n- The control arm's 31% matches your overall rate. That suggests the opt-in sample isn't unusual on this outcome.\n- Three weeks of two engineers is a small, reversible cost. A further study would likely take as long as the build and mostly repeat what you already know.\n\n**What the email result doesn't tell you:**\n- Push is a different channel. It may be more immediate, but it's easier to dismiss, and some patients will have notifications off.\n- Email opt-in patients may differ from app users who enable push.\n- It was one quarter, so seasonality is possible.\n\nSo expect an effect that is probably smaller than 13 points, and treat the size as unknown.\n\n**How to build it:**\n1. Randomize from day one: push reminder versus no reminder, with a persistent holdout. Measure late collection from pharmacy records, as you did before.\n2. Set the ship/expand decision rule now. For example, expand if the late rate falls by at least 4–5 points.\n3. Check the push-permission rate among repeat-prescription patients first. If few have push enabled, reach limits the gain, and that could change the priority.\n4. Reuse the email timing and wording to keep the test focused on the channel.\n\nThe build is the experiment, and you get the answer without a separate research phase."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3197,"cache_read_input_tokens":5027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3197},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"526d17cd-b505-439a-874d-088ac0a28697","uuid":"c7b6956d-f355-4f5b-8b74-e145bed8b2bd","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:18:15.261Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1u4gHQB9q8jHdC9oaw"}
